<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Once we were in old Chaldea,</l><l>Worshipping the idols there;</l><l>But the God of glory called us,</l><l>Saved us all from Satan’s snare.</l><l>Get out, get out, from Chaldea,</l><l>From that evil foreign land.</l><l>Come in, come in, to the good land,</l><l>Christ, the church, the one new man.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>With the calling comes the promise</l><l>Of the kingdom life on earth.</l><l>This becomes our strength and motive</l><l>To get out of all the dearth!</l><l>Lord, we’re crossing every river—</l><l>For this You must call us on,</l><l>Till Your kingdom and expression</l><l>On this earth are fully come.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>This is now the highest gospel</l><l>To those still in Chaldee’s land—</l><l>Leave the fallen situation,</l><l>You’ve been chosen for God’s plan.</l><l>God of glory, God of glory,</l><l>Do appear to us each day,</l><l>Call us out into Your building,</l><l>Your desire on earth today.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
